s":[],"scenes":[{"id":78269859631540,"name":"Lo-fi pop","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1990,"end":2002,"desc":"El gran invento de los independientes neozelandeses se convierte en uno de los fenómenos mundiales de los noventa: Cakekitchen, Bailter Space, Underground Lovers, King Loser; en Australia, Blackeyed Susans y Moles. En EE UU, Olympia (Beat Happening, Some Velvet Sidewalk, Spinanes), Modest Mouse y, sobre todo, Pavement, el grupo lo-fi más influyente (Slanted And Enchanted), con su contagio por todo el país (Silver Jews, Crowsdell). La vertiente más creativa, heredera de Half Japanese y los Residents: Trumans Water, Velocity Girl, Heavy Vegetable, Quintron, Danielson Famile, Soul Junk.","color":"#f472b6","family":"Pop, power-pop y synth-pop","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#lofi-pop"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":54006819131534,"artist":"Silver Jews","artist_id":211911945599465,"title":"Starlite Walker","year":1994,"ess":0,"yt":"W13_sh0bwXA","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Lo-fi pop","scene_id":78269859631540,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#lofi-pop","chapters":["Sección 6.5"],"pages":[[1,246,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":246,"text":"…Kansas (Butterglory) to Virginia (Wingtip Sloat), from Oregon (Crabs) to Chicago (Number One Cup), to Toronto (Dinner Is Ruined). David Berman's Silver Jews (1) coined a \"lo-fi\" version of the Velvet Underground's boogie-trance, like a cross between Luna and Pavement, on Starlite Walker (1994). Shannon…"}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Home Recordings (Early 1990s)","body":"This New Jersey-based band exemplified the lo-fi approach by recording their songs into a cheap machine that simply sat on top of their television. This rudimentary setup highlights their commi